      "issue": "Readiness probe uses tcpSocket on port 'http' instead of the application's /ready endpoint. A TCP check can pass while the process is CPU-throttled or unable to serve requests, so the Pod remains Ready during application-level degradation.",
      "severity": "medium"
    }
  ],
  "suspicious_resources": [
    "Deployment/api"
  ],
  "significant_events": [],
  "preliminary_assessment": "Service/api selector and targetPort match Deployment/api, and ConfigMap/code is mounted correctly. The primary verified misconfiguration is the API container's 50m CPU limit against CPU_ITERATIONS=500000 and 4 requests/second load, which will cause CPU throttling and latency/timeouts. The tcpSocket readiness probe will not detect this application-level degradation. No Kubernetes events were provided, so event correlation is unobserved."
}

